\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Formal categorical generative-model schema. Source relation: source-inspired original schematic related to Friston et al.~(2024), Figs. 1 and 4; estimand: categorical dependency structure; uncertainty: none. The x-axis is the dependency or role order within each panel; the y-axis positions hidden states, observations, model factors, and optional context levels. Panel A shows a hidden 9-cell location and the corresponding categorical likelihood row \(A[o,s]\), making the private sensory report explicit. Panel B shows \(A\), \(B\), \(C\), and \(D_0\) feeding the local posterior \(q(s)\); Panel C shows temporal state, observation, posterior, and action order; Panel D shows optional top-down conditioned priors. The equation ribbon records the implemented state-inference form and the zero-robustness recovery identity. This deterministic formal schematic contains no fitted values, empirical sample, error band, or confidence interval.}}{15}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:generative-model-schema}{{4}{15}{Formal categorical generative-model schema. Source relation: source-inspired original schematic related to Friston et al.~(2024), Figs. 1 and 4; estimand: categorical dependency structure; uncertainty: none. The x-axis is the dependency or role order within each panel; the y-axis positions hidden states, observations, model factors, and optional context levels. Panel A shows a hidden 9-cell location and the corresponding categorical likelihood row \(A[o,s]\), making the private sensory report explicit. Panel B shows \(A\), \(B\), \(C\), and \(D_0\) feeding the local posterior \(q(s)\); Panel C shows temporal state, observation, posterior, and action order; Panel D shows optional top-down conditioned priors. The equation ribbon records the implemented state-inference form and the zero-robustness recovery identity. This deterministic formal schematic contains no fitted values, empirical sample, error band, or confidence interval}{figure.caption.31}{}}
